  "prompt_text": "Use case: style-transfer. Transform animal reference sheet into a complete game sprite sheet of the bird described below. Preserve2rows x5columns with exactly TEN whole figures of same individual. Reference1 animal family style/layout only; references2person and3scene locked style only. Transparent1536x1024 RGBA with wide gutters, margins; no labels/grid/background/shadows/ground/nests/eggs. Top row SOUTH front three-quarter35degrees viewerLEFT, bottom row EAST side three-quarter facingRIGHT, ~20degrees down camera, upper-left light. Natural-history fine sepia-black ink, major contour2x interior, restrained two-tone earthy wash. Feather marks only3groups of3short strokes directed upper-left to lower-right, broad quiet feather planes, no dense hatching. Same body size each upright pose, two anatomically correct attached legs/feet, robust connected toes and beak surviving small sprite reduction. BOTH ROWS columns:1STAND both feet grounded head alert;2WALK one foot conspicuously lifted bent knee other grounded;3RUN legs far apart in strong stride, body leaning forward with wings held close, visually different from walk;4GRAZE/PECK head down beak touching foot level with rump raised, no food drawn;5DEAD completely limp lying horizontal on side, neck and head flat, legs limp out sideways, eyes closed as short lines, no blood, never sleeping upright. Will be reduced to small96x80game canvas. SUBJECT: Primitive domestic CHICKEN HEN, muted buff-ochre and russet plumage, rounded but lean natural body, short fanned tail, small muted brick-red comb and wattles, parchment yellow short beak and ochre feet. No large rooster tail, no white industrial breed, no decorative costume. Earliest bronze-age livestock. STRICT MARK BUDGET: use smooth UNTEXTURED wash planes, no all-over fur ticks, no stipple, grain, freckled texture or scratchy shading. Internal material marks are at most THREE small separated clusters of THREE strokes; leave90percent of coat completely quiet. The outline can have a few broad fur points but no comb-like fringe. This sparse style constraint overrides any dense texture visible in references. Main contour2:1 to inner anatomical lines; eyes and joints minimal.\n",
